                    {
                        "sense_id": "a3d4019d-ab22-31c0-9c2b-eaa6640bd2c5",
                        "entry_id": "97d9e941-b803-3687-91a5-71449c3cae1d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To assimilate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9758a3b0-2de8-481e-b11d-75f86208af33",
                                "sense_id": "a3d4019d-ab22-31c0-9c2b-eaa6640bd2c5",
                                "text": "So that small and little vital Principle of the Fear of God doth gradually and yet suddenly assimulate the actions of our life flowing from another Principle"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "370c1d4d-bf29-4ce8-b836-b817124c75f0",
                                "sense_id": "a3d4019d-ab22-31c0-9c2b-eaa6640bd2c5",
                                "text": "You will remember the exact analogy — that trees grow by attracting and assimulating to themselves the terrestrial atmosphere which is thrown from all the planets[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f83b5a9-6433-33c0-b026-65bc24974a32",
                        "entry_id": "97d9e941-b803-3687-91a5-71449c3cae1d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To feign; to counterfeit; to simulate."
                        ],
